The Dynamic Island behaviour in assets/island.js is a port of islandcn:

    https://github.com/opencoredev/islandcn
    (commit 0011a41ea4882f3818caf35c98f3ee46b80c4a2c)
    MIT License, copyright (c) 2026 Leo

The ported math lives in spring.ts, path.ts, geometry.ts, metrics.ts, store.ts
and a motion-constants excerpt under docs/reference/islandcn/, kept alongside
this notice so every measured number stays traceable to its calibration note.

Changes made in this port: the code is plain JavaScript with no React and no
build step; the spring, continuous-corner path and layout rules are kept as
upstream solved them; the activity stack keeps the upstream rules but drops the
development tools, the group hand-off timers and the recorded-clip comparison;
the renderer is a fixed DOM template for seven content atoms instead of
arbitrary React nodes; glyphs are drawn for this site rather than taken from
Hugeicons; the gooey split neck is deferred to its own milestone. See
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-islandcn-dynamic-island-design.md section 10.

islandcn copies the look and motion of Apple's island, and so does this port,
but neither uses any Apple asset. Not affiliated with Apple; Dynamic Island is a
trademark of Apple Inc. and is not used as this feature's name in reader-facing
copy.
